# SwiftFormat configuration.
#
# There was no config here, so both swiftformat and swiftlint ran on defaults
# and the docs claimed `swiftformat --lint .` passed. It never did — a default
# run rewrote 67 of 115 files, including turning 44_100 into 44100 and putting
# every single-line `if` body on its own line.
#
# The rules disabled below are ones this codebase violates on purpose. They are
# turned off rather than "fixed" so that `--lint` means something: a failure now
# is drift worth looking at, not the house style losing an argument with a
# default.

--swiftversion 6.0

# Style the instrument uses deliberately.
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies      # single-line guard/if bodies are the norm here
--disable wrapPropertyBodies         # `var id: String { rawValue }` reads better on one line
--disable trailingCommas             # the effect-order arrays close without one
--disable numberFormatting           # 44_100 is a sample rate, not a number to regroup
--disable redundantSelf              # explicit self in os_log interpolation is required
--disable docComments                # `//` block comments above types are intentional
--disable conditionalAssignment
--disable redundantSwiftUIGroup
--disable environmentEntry
--disable redundantViewBuilder

# Whitespace and imports are enforced — they cannot change meaning and they are
# the difference between a readable diff and a noisy one.
